<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait credit extension rises in Feb.</title>
<headline>Kuwait credit extension rises in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Domestic credit extended by banks operating in Kuwait rose to 3.342 billion dinars at the end of February from 3.265 billion in January, Central Bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The credit amounted to 2.469 billion dinars at the end of February 1996.</p>
<p>Balance of cash portion used from domestic credit facilities by sector:</p>
<p>				Figures in million dinars</p>
<p>				     Feb '97		Feb '96</p>
<p>Trade				570.3		  423.0</p>
<p>Industry			   240.8		  200.2</p>
<p>Construction		     213.7		  154.9</p>
<p>Agriculture and Fishing	 10.8		    8.6</p>
<p>Non-bank financial</p>
<p> institutions		    170.5		  143.0</p>
<p>Personal Facilities	  1,530.2		1,135.3</p>
<p>Real Estate			434.0		  238.9</p>
<p>Other				171.3		  165.2</p>
<p>Total			    3,341.8		2,469.1</p>
<p> of which, consumer loans    503.4		  518.5</p>
<p>Note: Non-bank financial institutions include insurance, money exchange and investment firms. The figures include the effect of purchasing debts of Kuwaiti debtors in return for Debt Purchase Bonds since December 1991.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in totals are due to rounding.</p>
<p>-- Inal Ersan, +965 243-1920</p>
<p>($1 = 0.302 dinars)</p>
